= Dither designs from September 2026 (fba_dither_auto) =

== Overview ==

Two things happened in September 2026.

First, the April 2026 release (0.0.3) was found to produce designs in which only
a few hundred fibres landed on stars and the rest went to sky.  That was a
target-selection mismatch, fixed in 0.0.4 by `--stdsource`.

Second, it became clear that ''neither'' of the two existing scripts works
everywhere: the main-survey star catalog stops at Dec = -30, and the CMX one is
frozen at 2020 and yields almost no flux standards.  So 0.0.5 adds
'''`fba_dither_auto`''', a single self-contained script that probes the tile
centre and uses whichever set of catalogs actually has targets there.

For most work `fba_dither_auto` is now the script to run.  `fba_main_dither` and
`fba_cmx_new` remain for science tiles and for reference.

== Why the old designs were sparse ==

The dithering flavors selected their stars with the main survey `STD_FAINT` bit
(`DESI_TARGET` bit 33).  That is the survey's ''spectrophotometric calibration''
standard selection and is deliberately sparse -- of order 60 stars per square
degree, i.e. 450-1500 candidates on a tile.  Fiberassign cannot fill 5000 fibres
from that, so the rest went to sky.

The CMX script had used `STD_DITHER`, a dense Gaia star selection built for
dithering.  When the script was ported to the main survey in April 2026,
`STD_DITHER` was mapped onto `STD_FAINT`.  Both are called "standards", but they
do different jobs.  For the record, `STD_DITHER` is only `gaiagmag >= 11.5` and
`gaiarmag >= 11.5` -- no colour cuts, no faint limit -- so the true main-survey
analogue is `GAIA_STD_FAINT` ''plus'' the `BACKUP_*` bits, not `GAIA_STD_FAINT`
alone.

It went unnoticed because every validated test case in 0.0.3 was ''outside'' the
DR9 footprint (RA=250 Dec=-5, RA=190 Dec=-25).  Off-footprint the script already
fell back to the Gaia catalog, which is dense, so every tested tile looked
healthy.  The first genuinely in-footprint dither tiles were the September 2026
high-elevation designs, and those are the ones that failed.

== fba_dither_auto ==

Self-contained: it shells out to nothing, and takes no `--dtver` and no
`--stdsource`.  Dither flavors only (`dithprec`, `dithlost`, `dithfocus`);
science tiles stay in `fba_main_dither`.

It probes the tile centre and chooses:

{{{
main   GAIA_STD_FAINT, gaiadr2/1.0.0 backup        if >= --min-targets
cmx    STD_DITHER (dr9/0.49.0 cmx no-obscon), or
       STD_DITHER_GAIA (gaiadr2/0.49.0 cmx supp)   otherwise
}}}

The threshold asks about the '''main path only''': can the main-survey catalog
fill this focal plane?  If yes, prefer it -- its catalogs are current and every
assigned star is a flux standard.  If no, fall to CMX, which is ~10x denser
everywhere but frozen at 2020 and assigns almost no standards (127 against 833
at RA=46 Dec=+2).

`--min-targets` defaults to '''9000''', roughly where a design saturates the
4354 assignable fibres.  It is a preference, not a maximum: CMX is denser at
336 +30 (61103 against 9146) and is still not chosen there.

=== Nothing is gated on the DESI footprint ===

Both the main/CMX choice and the CMX `no-obscon`/`supp` choice come from probing
the catalogs, not from `is_point_in_desi()`.  That test answers a different
question: a tile can sit ''inside'' the footprint and still have no coverage in
the catalog the footprint test would pick.  RA=305 Dec=-20 is the worked
example -- `tile_in_desi = 1`, but `no-obscon` holds '''0''' `STD_DITHER` while
`supp` holds '''70745''' `STD_DITHER_GAIA`.  Under the old logic that tile failed
outright.

=== Decisions at the September 2026 centres ===

|| '''centre''' || '''main''' || '''cmx''' || '''cmx supp''' || '''chosen''' ||
|| 336 +30 || 9146 || 61103 || 54657 || main ||
||   0 +30 || 3111 || 31850 || -- || cmx ||
||  15 +30 || 2514 || 24619 || -- || cmx ||
||  46  +2 || 1268 || 13422 || 12566 || cmx ||
||  46  -2 || 1206 || 12858 || 11671 || cmx ||
|| 305 -20 || 17238 || '''0''' || 70745 || main ||
||  80 -40 || '''0''' || 30554 || 25823 || cmx ||

=== It reproduces both original scripts exactly ===

Same centre, seed and rundate (science / science-not-standard / standard / sky):

|| '''path''' || '''fba_dither_auto''' || '''original''' ||
|| CMX, 46 +2 || 3869 / 3742 / 127 / 450 || `fba_cmx_new`: identical ||
|| main, 336 +30 || 3439 / 3439 / 394 || `fba_main_dither`: identical ||

The dithering machinery was already byte-identical between the two scripts, so
what the merged script carries per path is configuration -- catalog directories,
`dtver`, target bits, the `survey=` string, the tile obscon (`DARK|GRAY|BRIGHT`
on the CMX path), the `--gaia_stdmask` value, and the `main_cmx_or_sv` monkey
patch on the CMX path only.

== Where each path works ==

A sky map of both catalogs is in the repository at
`skymap/dither_coverage.png`.

'''`GAIA_STD_FAINT` stops dead at Dec = -30''' -- the DESI footprint's southern
limit.  Zero, not thinning.

|| '''Dec band''' || '''CMX usable''' || '''main usable''' ||
|| -90 to -60 || 100% || '''0%''' ||
|| -60 to -40 || 100% || '''0%''' ||
|| -40 to -30 || 97% || 11% ||
|| -35 to -25 || 97% || 52% ||
|| -30 to -20 || 98% || 95% ||
||   0 to +20 || 100% || 99% ||

At >= 1000 targets per tile: 73% of sky either path works, '''27% CMX-only'''
(almost all the southern cap, plus the Galactic plane and the Magellanic
Clouds), and 0% main-only.  Below Dec = -30 the CMX path is not a preference, it
is the only option.

== Known limitation: the CMX sky budget ==

CMX designs read `dr9/0.49.0` skies, which are far sparser than `1.0.0`: 6-18
sky fibres per petal at 80 -40, and '''0''' at 305 -20, against the 40 requested
by `--nskypet`.  This is accepted, not a bug to chase.  `verify_design.py`
reports it as a NOTE and still passes the design.

== Environment: pin desimodules/26.3 ==

'''`desimodules/main` cannot run these scripts as of September 2026.'''  It
ships numpy 2.5.3, under which `desitarget.io.write_mtl` fails on ''every'' MTL
write: it does `int(np.unique(release // 1000))`, and converting a size-1
`ndim > 0` array to a Python scalar raises `TypeError` from numpy 2.4 on.
`write_mtl` catches it and re-raises the misleading
`"Multiple data releases in MTL ([9])"` -- where `[9]` is a ''single'' release.
A minimal reproducer is in the repository at
`dither_20260921/repro_write_mtl_numpy2.py`.

The scripts probe for this at startup and exit with an actionable message rather
than failing several hundred log lines into the run.  Until desitarget is fixed,
source the pinned release.

== Running the script ==

{{{
source /global/common/software/desi/desi_environment.sh 26.3

./fba_dither_auto --tilera 46 --tiledec -2 --tileid 84182 \
  --faflavor dithprec --rundate 2026-09-23T10:00:00+00:00 \
  --seed 80 --outdir ./084/
}}}

`--dry-run` reports the decision and exits in about five seconds, which is light
enough for a login node.  `--force main|cmx` skips the probe.  `--min-targets`
moves the bar.

A full design (1 reference tile + 12 dithers) takes 3-5 minutes and writes about
300 MB, so run it inside an allocation:

{{{
salloc --no-shell -A desi -C cpu -q interactive -t 04:00:00 -N 1 -J dither
JID=$(squeue -u $USER -h -n dither -o "%i")
srun --jobid=$JID -n1 -c 32 ./fba_dither_auto ...
}}}

== Verifying a design ==

Check the written products rather than the log:

{{{
python dither_20260921/verify_design.py <outdir> <reference tileid>
}}}

It handles designs from either path -- the survey is read off the `FIBERASSIGN`
columns -- and reports per tile the assigned fibres, fibres on stars and sky, and
`EXTRA` HDU placement, then the per-petal sky budget and the realised dither
scatter.  It exits non-zero if anything is wrong.

== Repository information ==

The scripts and full changelog are in the GitHub release:
https://github.com/forero/dither_DESI/releases/tag/0.0.5

== Checking tiles into SVN ==

Tiles with TILEIDs starting with 084 should be checked into svn.

'''Check out into its own directory, never into a directory that already holds
other work.'''  `svn co <url> .` in a shared area such as `$SCRATCH` turns that
whole area into a working copy, after which `svn status` reports every unrelated
project directory as unversioned.

{{{
mkdir -p ~/tiles && cd ~/tiles
svn co https://desi.lbl.gov/svn/data/tiles/trunk/084
cd 084
}}}

Copy in the designs and add them '''by name''', not with a blanket add:

{{{
cp /path/to/designs/fiberassign-0841??.fits.gz .
cp /path/to/designs/fiberassign-0841??.png .
svn add fiberassign-0841??.fits.gz fiberassign-0841??.png
svn status            # read this before committing
svn commit -m "Add dithprec fiberassign designs for tileids 084104-084181"
}}}

Do '''not''' use `svn status | grep '^?' | xargs svn add`: it adds everything
unversioned under the current directory, which is safe only if the working copy
contains nothing else.

The last tileid committed is '''084103'''; the September 2026 designs took
084104-084181, so the next free block starts at '''084182'''.

You can browse the committed files at:
https://desi.lbl.gov/svn/data/tiles/trunk/084/
